      "info": {
        "title": "zombie-settlement-3ds",
        "author": "JustGoodinc",
        "description": "Top-down pixel-art zombie survival + settlement game for Windows and Nintendo 3DS (homebrew)",
        "category": [
          "homebrew"
        ],
        "console": [
          "3DS"
        ],
        "version": "v0.4.2",
        "license": "MIT",
        "last_updated": "2026-11-11 at 07:08 (UTC)",
        "releasenotes": "v0.4.2 (2026-11-11)\nv0.4.2 — X takes everything\n- In a container, X takes everything (Take All), on the 3DS and with a pad. The footer shows it.\n\nInstall\n- Windows: unzip and run StayingAlive.exe\n- 3DS Homebrew Launcher: copy the .3dsx to sdmc:/3ds/\n- 3DS HOME Menu: install the .cia with FBI (scan StayingAlive-FBI-QR.png via Remote Install > Scan QR Code). See docs/FBI_INSTALLATION.md.\n\nHardware status: the 3DS build has been booted in the Azahar emulator only; real-hardware and QR installs are not yet verified.\n\n----------\n\nv0.4.1 (2026-11-11)\nv0.4.1 — 30 fps on the Old 3DS\n- Graphics setting (Settings, on the 3DS): Auto (Fast on an Old 3DS, Full on a New 3DS), Full or Fast. Fast shows the settlement at raid zoom instead of one step further out, skips the settlement colour grade, and while you play redraws the touch screen at 15 fps (at once for the stylus, START, SELECT, A and B). Prompted by the owner's test on an Old 3DS XL: v0.4.0 ran at about 20 fps.\n- Faster for everyone, with no visible change: the 2x scale-up of the world view writes two pixels at a time and copies repeated rows; the copy to the rotated 3DS screens moves eight rows at a time (checked pixel-exact against the old copy); the zombie sprites of a level are drawn while it loads, not the first time each zombie comes into view.\n- In the emulator's Old 3DS mode a frame now costs 9.9-13.4 ms with Fast graphics against 16.0-20.9 ms in v0.4.0 (about half at the settlement, a third less on a raid). Not yet measured on a console: see docs/NINTENDO_3DS_BUILD.md, which also explains the new bench file that makes the game measure itself on a console and write perf.txt.\n\nInstall\n- Windows: unzip and run StayingAlive.exe\n- 3DS Homebrew Launcher: copy the .3dsx to sdmc:/3ds/\n- 3DS HOME Menu: install the .cia with FBI (scan StayingAlive-FBI-QR.png via Remote Install > Scan QR Code). See docs/FBI_INSTALLATION.md.\n\nHardware status: the 3DS build has been booted in the Azahar emulator only; real-hardware and QR installs are not yet verified.\n\n----------\n\nv0.4.0 (2026-11-11)\nv0.4.0 — a new first hour (tutorial, soundtrack, raids) and the visual overhaul\n- New tutorial. A new game opens with a short scene at the settlement (the fire, the radio, the leader's decision, the walk to the gate, a title card) and goes straight out on a first raid of the police station, alone. Lessons finish when you do the thing, with the button to press drawn in the text and a gold marker on what the lesson points at: move, search the marked car, Take All, open the backpack, fight, reload, dodge, extract. The marked car always holds the same useful first haul. The two zombies of the fight lesson bite weakly and cannot infect, so a first fight cannot end the run; everything else on that raid plays by the normal rules. Back home a second scene takes the camera round the six buildings, then you upgrade one with what you brought back, and the last lesson points at the next raid. A/Next moves a scene on, START skips the scene, Skip Tutorial skips everything. Replay it from Settings.\n- Expeditions are now raids everywhere in the game (the Raid button, Raid Prep, Raid Failed, the objective and journal lines).\n- A soundtrack: slow, and written as horror. Seven original pieces for a small synthesiser, one for the menus and one for each place. None of them keeps a beat. Each is a low drone that throbs, string chords that slide into place and sit a semitone wrong, one sparse figure, a held note, and a sound that belongs to the place:\n  - Dead Air (menus): a heartbeat, chords sinki...",
        "wiki": "https://github.com/JustGoodinc/zombie-settlement-3ds"
      }
    },
