      "info": {
        "title": "sh-3ds",
        "author": "platonovns",
        "description": "Native Silent Hill (1999) port on nintendo new 3ds (based on pc port)",
        "category": [
          "homebrew"
        ],
        "console": [
          "3DS"
        ],
        "version": "sh-3ds-v0.9.1.1",
        "license": "GPL-3.0",
        "last_updated": "2026-11-04 at 18:16 (UTC)",
        "releasenotes": "sh-3ds-v0.9.1.1 (2026-11-04)\nSH-3DS v0.9.1.1\n\nThis update to v0.9.1 ships the verified New Nintendo 3DS build with the project's recommended starting settings for controls, map brightness and other gameplay options. Fresh defaults include Hybrid controls, 40% map brightness, 60 FPS gameplay pacing, the map enabled, HP LED, HUD off, and automatic lower-screen management. You can adjust these settings in the pause menu. Existing saved settings take precedence over fresh defaults.\n\nThe attached binaries are the previously verified v0.9.1 build, renamed for this release; their internal version metadata remains v0.9.1. No game code was changed for this publication.\n\nGame data\n\nRequires your own legally obtained Silent Hill NTSC-U (USA), SLUS-00707 v1.1 disc image. Place the raw single-track MODE2/2352 image and its CUE at sdmc:/3ds/silenthill/sh1.bin and sdmc:/3ds/silenthill/sh1.cue. The required disc image is not supplied. New Nintendo 3DS family systems are the supported target.\n\nSHA-256\n\ntext\n9aaaa269dfab4e0c9bb4ba8a70d39fecf13e79d7cce9b348dce46c8e762ddc81  SH-3DS-v0.9.1.1.3dsx\nf54965942a3f2013cccb425d3efc44a45ff9dc1172aef149eb5422bd040d9bec  SH-3DS-v0.9.1.1.cia\n\n----------\n\nsh-3ds (2026-11-01)\nSH-3DS — First Public Release\n\nCompatibility / testing\n\nThe game has been played from beginning to end on a real New Nintendo 3DS.\n\nMy complete playthrough used the Good+ ending. Other endings have not yet been personally tested, so please report any issues you encounter.\n\nThis is the first public release, so there may still be bugs or hardware-specific issues that I haven't encountered during testing.\n\nGame data\n\nSH-3DS does not include any original Silent Hill game data.\n\nYou must provide the game image from your own legally obtained copy of Silent Hill.\n\nCurrently, SH-3DS supports the NTSC-U (USA) SLUS-00707 v1.1 release.\n\nPlace the following files on your SD card:\n\nsdmc:/3ds/silenthill/sh1.bin\nsdmc:/3ds/silenthill/sh1.cue\n\nThe filenames must be exactly sh1.bin and sh1.cue.\n\nFeedback\n\nBug reports are welcome. If you encounter a problem, please include where it happened, what you were doing, and whether the issue can be reproduced.",
        "wiki": "https://github.com/platonovns/sh-3ds"
      }
    },
